# Multi-Armed Bandit RL Project

![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.8%2B-blue.svg)
![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)
![Topic](https://img.shields.io/badge/Topic-Reinforcement%20Learning-orange.svg)

## 📌 Project Overview
This project delivers a modular, object-oriented comparative analysis of foundational **Multi-Armed Bandit (MAB)** exploration-exploitation strategies in Reinforcement Learning. Using a standard 10-armed Gaussian testbed ($k=10$), the project evaluates and benchmarks four core decision-making agents over 1,000 simulation steps:

1. **Random Agent:** Uniform random action selection baseline.
2. **$\epsilon$-Greedy Agent:** Balances exploitation ($\arg\max Q(a)$) with fixed exploration ($\epsilon=0.1$).
3. **Softmax Agent:** Probabilistic action selection using the Boltzmann distribution ($\tau=0.1$).
4. **Upper Confidence Bound (UCB) Agent:** Deterministic exploration guided by uncertainty upper bounds ($c=0.2$).

